5. System Architecture

PhonePrint consists of three major components.

A. Mobile Application

The mobile application is responsible for:

- User interface
- Device registration
- Biometric authentication
- Secure key management
- Authentication challenge signing

B. Windows Agent

The Windows Agent is responsible for:

- Device management
- Secure communication
- Challenge generation
- Signature verification
- Authentication request handling

C. Windows Credential Provider

The Windows Credential Provider is the planned native integration responsible for connecting PhonePrint with the Windows sign-in experience.

It must work with a supported Windows authentication mechanism and must not bypass Windows security.

